17592186045454 13194139533651 true] [17592186244245 1111 #uuid "b725bcb7-48c3-5a89-a727-bba23109152a" 13194139533651 true] [17592186244246 1034 "I only" 13194139533651 true] [17592186244246 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139533651 true] [17592186244246 1111 #uuid "2293c12a-9691-5dcf-8ad1-908149ea758b" 13194139533651 true] [17592186244247 1034 "III only" 13194139533651 true] [17592186244247 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139533651 true] [17592186244247 1111 #uuid "1d4035ce-18b3-5f39-aa32-182e76f979f1" 13194139533651 true] [17592186244248 1034 "I and II only" 13194139533651 true] [17592186244248 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139533651 true] [17592186244248 1111 #uuid "c6f4dce8-7d34-5d0a-a308-f9b3b6b7b327" 13194139533651 true] [17592186244249 1017 #edb/ref 17592186244250 13194139533651 true] [17592186244249 1089 "q-66669" 13194139533651 true] [17592186244249 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139533651 true] [17592186244249 1100 "Given that $f(x)=(x-2{)}^{2},$ on which of the following intervals is $f(x)$ invertible?\n\n- $x\\in (2,\\infty )$\n- $x\\in (-1,5)$\n- $x\\in (-\\infty ,2]$" 13194139533651 true] [17592186244249 1113 #uuid "8d503350-373b-552d-8a35-6045ac022068" 13194139533651 true] [17592186244249 1138 false 13194139533651 true] [17592186244249 1145 "The graph of the function $f(x)=(x-2{)}^{2},$ can be obtained in the following way:\n\n- Take the curve $y={x}^{2}.$\n\n- Translate it by $2$ units  to  the right  $f(x)=(x-2{)}^{2}.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13932058/assets/1e3ac550e35a3dc93b3e26e5834f763847b04f5133de02e368124f54dd2b9dd6.png)\n\nA function is invertible on a particular interval if and only if it's a one-to-one function on that interval. To determine the intervals on which the function is invertible, we use the horizontal line test.\n\n- The function $f(x)$ is not invertible on the interval $x\\in (-1,5).$ On this interval, some horizontal lines will intersect the curve more than once.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13932058/assets/3ebb316ca122b6786b8ef501fc7c56f8e0e68c8cfc32e5801c493d38382fc26c.png)\n\n- The function $f(x)$ is invertible on the intervals $x\\in (2,\\infty )$  and $x\\in (-\\infty ,2].$  On these intervals, any horizontal line will intersect the curve at most once, no matter where we draw the line.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13932058/assets/86c7c9cacc7a3868565f33130563ffed0ca423aa087e76cc08d103ea171822ed.png)\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and III only\"." 13194139533651 true] [17592186244250 1000 #edb/ref 17592186244251 13194139533651 true] [17592186244250 1000 #edb/ref 17592186244252 13194139533651 true] [17592186244250 1000 #edb/ref 17592186244253 13194139533651 true] [17592186244250 1000 #edb/ref 17592186244254 13194139533651 true] [17592186244250 1000 #edb/ref 17592186244255 13194139533651 true] [17592186244250 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139533651 true] [17592186244250 1041 "selection" 13194139533651 true] [17592186244250 1104 #edb/ref 17592186244252 13194139533651 true] [17592186244250 1110 #uuid "115f5585-6883-54bd-9a38-1df84dfaba64" 13194139533651 true] [17592186244251 1034 "II and III only" 13194139533651 true] [17592186244251 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139533651 true] [17592186244251 1111 #uuid "0f299779-9645-5fec-9d18-5081087bfaf9" 13194139533651 true] [17592186244252 1034 "I and III only" 13194139533651 true] [17592186244252 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139533651 true] [17592186244252 1111 #uuid "3ebe1cc4-44ed-568a-8cfc-08b9188b8187" 13194139533651 true] [17592186244253 1034 "I only" 13194139533651 true] [17592186244253 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139533651 true] [17592186244253 1111 #uuid "7a35e99c-1b0e-5efc-bb12-73dbbc9be9ca" 13194139533651 true] [17592186244254 1034 "III only" 13194139533651 true] [17592186244254 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139533651 true] [17592186244254 1111 #uuid "0cd370f6-3c93-5eda-9eac-539bb3a27499" 13194139533651 true] [17592186244255 1034 "II only" 13194139533651 true] [17592186244255 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139533651 true] [17592186244255 1111 #uuid "1e600908-bcb8-5927-9a9e-62b963ec33b6" 13194139533651 true] [17592186244256 1017 #edb/ref 17592186244257 13194139533651 true] [17592186244256 1089 "q-66725" 13194139533651 true] [17592186244256 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139533651 true] [17592186244256 1100 "Given that $f(x)=-x+3,$ on which of the following intervals is $f(x)$ invertible?\n\n- $x\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )$\n- $x\\in (0.5,\\infty )$\n- $x\\in [-3,\\sqrt{2}]$" 13194139533651 true] [17592186244256 1113 #uuid "dd254a1a-f8a4-5f4b-b81d-c5dcb8bdc11d" 13194139533651 true] [17592186244256 1138 false 13194139533651 true] [17592186244256 1145 "The function $f(x)$ is a linear function with slope $-1$ and $y$-intercept $3,$ as shown below. \n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13932058/assets/aaa05d1ab0fd630dacd81723fe00472cb901fb6f73af5f111f44459476191c0f.png)\n\nA function is invertible on a particular interval if and only if it's a one-to-one function on that interval. To determine the intervals on which the function is invertible, we use the horizontal line test.\n\n- The given function is invertible on the interval $x\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).$ On this interval, a horizontal line will intersect the curve at most once, no matter where we draw the line.\n\n- Since the function is invertible on $x\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ),$ it is also invertible on  $x\\in (0.5,\\infty )$ and $x\\in [-3,\\sqrt{2}].$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I, II, and III\"." 13194139533651 true] [17592186244257 1000 #edb/ref 17592186244258 13194139533651 true] [17592186244257 1000 #edb/ref 17592186244259 13194139533651 true] [17592186244257 1000 #edb/ref 17592186244260 13194139533651 true] [17592186244257 1000 #edb/ref 17592186244261 13194139533651 true] [17592186244257 1000 #edb/ref 17592186244262 13194139533651 true] [17592186244257 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139533651 true] [17592186244257 1041 "selection" 13194139533651 true] [17592186244257 1104 #edb/ref 17592186244258 13194139533651 true] [17592186244257 1110 #uuid "53edd5a3-e1a4-57f0-a8a0-071b51fb43c8" 13194139533651 true] [17592186244258 1034 "I, II, and III" 13194139533651 true] [17592186244258 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139533651 true] [17592186244258 1111 #uuid "7f6cf143-cbdc-53bf-8cd1-7055de3b64df" 13194139533651 true] [17592186244259 1034 "I only" 13194139533651 true] [17592186244259 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139533651 true] [17592186244259 1111 #uuid "eb199e1f-3386-5f7f-a3fd-e27d1aa32736" 13194139533651 true] [17592186244260 1034 "III only" 13194139533651 true] [17592186244260 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139533651 true] [17592186244260 1111 #uuid "bd213512-1733-556a-b244-e6486893704f" 13194139533651 true] [17592186244261 1034 "I and II only" 13194139533651 true] [17592186244261 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139533651 true] [17592186244261 1111 #uuid "f9086544-2c0f-52ec-ad94-5f2f5f708ed9" 13194139533651 true] [17592186244262 1034 "II only" 13194139533651 true] [17592186244262 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139533651 true] [17592186244262 1111 #uuid "514b617e-1470-5d45-ba92-53fbff4f153d" 13194139533651 true] [17592186244263 1017 #edb/ref 17592186244264 13194139533651 true] [17592186244263 1089 "q-66778" 13194139533651 true] [17592186244263 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139533651 true] [17592186244263 1100 "Given that $f(x)=|x+1|-3,$ on which of the following intervals is $f(x)$ invertible?\n\n- $x\\in (-\\infty ,1]$\n- $x\\in [1,\\infty )$\n- $x\\in (-\\infty ,-1]$" 13194139533651 true] [17592186244263 1113 #uuid "4fb981fb-d1de-5cf1-a91e-ec4693f30623" 13194139533651 true] [17592186244263 1138 false 13194139533651 true] [17592186244263 1145 "The graph of the function $f(x)=|x+1|-3$ can be obtained in the following way:\n\n- Take the curve $y=|x|.$\n\n- Translate it by $1$ units to the left,  to get $y=|x+1|.$\n\n- Finally, translate $y=|x+1|$ by $3$ units down to get $f(x)=|x+1|-3.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13932058/assets/3b9f56280089991c7db7652d84a777edd5c5e012921f0d48362f4fc3e4fd2a6e.png)\n\nA function is invertible on a particular interval if and only if it's a one-to-one function on that interval. To determine the intervals on which the function is invertible, we use the horizontal line test. \n\n- The function $f(x)$ is invertible on each of the intervals $x\\in (-\\infty ,-1]$ and $x\\in [1,\\infty ).$ On these intervals, a horizontal line will intersect the curve at most once, no matter where we draw the line.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13932058/assets/fd0b0fe70e009f43e80b0f712b6cfd576deb4c4c0457f61adae04cf7e44f140c.png)\n\n  \n\n- The function $f(x)$ is not invertible on the interval $x\\in (-\\infty ,1].$ On this interval, some horizontal lines will intersect the curve more than once.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13932058/assets/582ec1960b053731bf201c84d8c58fd4e1734a2b085cd5549a01aace4b600b4a.png)\n\n \n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II and III only\"." 13194139533651 true] [17592186244264 1000 #edb/ref 17592186244265 13194139533651 true] [17592186244264 1000 #edb/ref 17592186244266 13194139533651 true] [17592186244264 1000 #edb/ref 17592186244267 13194139533651 true] [17592186244264 1000 #edb/ref 17592186244268 13194139533651 true] [17592186244264 1000 #edb/ref 17592186244269 13194139533651 true] [17592186244264 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139533651 true] [17592186244264 1041 "selection" 13194139533651 true] [17592186244264 1104 #edb/ref 17592186244265 13194139533651 true] [17592186244264 1110 #uuid "a8456194-4870-5651-9907-46e558f25a6a" 13194139533651 true] [17592186244265 1034 "II and III only" 1319